## Threshold analysis: why one cut-off is not the decision

```python
display(pd.read_csv(run / "threshold_analysis.csv")[["threshold", "precision", "recall", "f1"]].round(3))
display(pd.read_csv(run / "threshold_business.csv"))
display(read_json(run / "break_even.json")["break_even_probability_quantiles"])
```

**Interpretation.** The F1-best threshold ({{ model.threshold | num(2) }}) treats every customer alike. With value and cost included, the churn probability at which an offer pays off differs by customer, from about {{ break_even.break_even_probability_quantiles.p10 | pct(0) }} for the most valuable to above 100% for the least valuable. Contacting everyone above the F1 threshold spends more and earns less than contacting everyone with positive expected value.

